DXSPIDER WEB ADMIN - INSTALLATION
=================================

This procedure installs DXWeb Admin only. Normal User Web is optional and
has a separate installation guide in dxweb/INSTALL.

Prerequisite: DXSpider and its standard dependencies are already installed.
The local DXSpider IntMsg listener must accept the #WEB transport on
127.0.0.1:27754 (or the port configured for this deployment). DXSpider
must provide the matching Web.pm and administrative backend capabilities.

The Git checkout must contain /spider/dxweb-admin/admin.pl, lib/ and
admin/. The service definition is supplied as /spider/dxweb-admin.service.

Install and start the service (run as root):

    cd /spider
    install -m 0644 dxweb-admin.service \
        /etc/systemd/system/dxweb-admin.service
    systemctl daemon-reload
    systemctl enable --now dxweb-admin.service

For direct access (without a reverse proxy):

    MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=0

The service starts /spider/dxweb-admin/admin.pl with:

    DXS_PORT=27754
    DXWEB_HOST=0.0.0.0
    DXWEB_PORT=7381

The DXSpider transport itself remains local at 127.0.0.1.

Direct mode
-----------

The defaults expose DXWeb Admin directly on TCP port 7381:

    DXWEB_HOST=0.0.0.0
    DXWEB_PORT=7381

Leave MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY unset (or set it to 0) when clients connect
directly to DXWeb Admin.

Reverse-proxy mode
------------------

A tested Nginx layout keeps the public port unchanged and moves the
application listener to a loopback-only backend:

    public/Nginx :7381 -> DXWeb Admin 127.0.0.1:7481

Configure DXWeb Admin with:

    DXWEB_HOST=127.0.0.1
    DXWEB_PORT=7481
    MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1

Nginx must proxy WebSocket upgrades and replace, rather than trust,
client-supplied forwarding headers. For example:

    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

With MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1 the backend listener is a security boundary:
do not expose TCP 7481 directly to untrusted clients. Only the trusted
reverse proxy should be able to reach it.

Edit the unit and reload systemd if the configured ports differ.

Verify only this service:

    systemctl status dxweb-admin.service --no-pager
    curl -i http://127.0.0.1:7381/healthz
    curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7381/admin-version.json

The version endpoint reports the application version running from this
checkout. /healthz returns HTTP 200 and state=ready once the DXSpider
link is established;
otherwise it may return HTTP 503. Test SYSOP Login/Logout in the browser.

DXWeb User does not need to be installed for Web Admin to operate.

Configuration diagrams (Spanish / English):
  /spider/dxweb/docs/DXWeb_Configuration_ES.png
  /spider/dxweb/docs/DXWeb_Configuration_EN.png
See /spider/dxweb/docs/README-nginx for the example reverse-proxy setup.
DXSpider WebCluster uses the IntMsg listener (normally 127.0.0.1:27754),
not the traditional DXSpider client/node listener.
